789888375319469540-3d9a26cd-6831-4a66-ae2e-7fe7888391b4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a7b405f84cc5ad0a21503d498578c3dc1b313a9c9bfecb1ce5d92f1a55e9ebe2","event_uuid":"fca05450-ee39-475d-805e-99ca1c41be1c","position":{"commit_sha":"45c84e0d20ed6e3df2ac223f82633f8dab53819c","position":"1789888415379318898-fca05450-ee39-475d-805e-99ca1c41be1c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a5ba7a635e884e9ad3c8100f8b6a0a5ec9a3262f1e32ed9823bf5df29575e820","event_uuid":"d0759e9b-7637-48bc-b53f-eefef0e544fe","position":{"commit_sha":"e4030667ff065b82698022a49d05be173fa99368","position":"1789889004865535146-d0759e9b-7637-48bc-b53f-eefef0e544fe"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"570fe940eb145939c3c0299d3135a69fb352728466031e5ad56d9dc2bf48c365","event_uuid":"389d9636-00b4-468a-8d65-446a365f5b26","position":{"commit_sha":"7f6c3a1ee2e6dfcd9dc891c11140959304edcb24","position":"1789889012484172871-389d9636-00b4-468a-8d65-446a365f5b26"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0bec20a0169e01998079d3c0a1aebd795f1672fbe66f04fc28ee1b45491b8a9f","event_uuid":"9084618e-d36d-4053-ab5b-81b7e4a6ec32","position":{"commit_sha":"526e9aebdead2fbf5a3ccabed0f6ed5997e02bd7","position":"1789889042297868656-9084618e-d36d-4053-ab5b-81b7e4a6ec32"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"plan_defect","comments":[],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1789782376063435495,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1d94ae0d-3387-47f0-8b96-560088c9bfe3","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8d27-d715-0611-48e3"},{"link_uuid":"934b883f-c76d-4f1b-9bc5-b4afdb6ef90b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d635-9e7f-2bea-4ebe"}],"description":"## Context\n\nFound by the `LLM-Review` bot on Gerrit change 2984 patchset 8 as three advisory findings. They were kept out of that change's scope so the cap-handler change could land without another scope expansion. All three defects are in `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py` on `origin/main`.\n\n## Confirmed defects\n\n**1. `_ce_spend_today` raises `KeyError` on a no-data period.** Lines 347-357 call Cost Explorer and treat only a missing `ResultsByTime` list as zero. Line 357 then indexes `results[0][\"Total\"][\"UnblendedCost\"][\"Amount\"]`, so a nonempty period with an empty or absent `Total` raises `KeyError`. That exception is outside the `ClientError` fallback in `handler()` lines 493-505, so it escapes instead of reusing a cached Cost Explorer signal.\n\n**2. The Cost Explorer poll gate bypasses `CE_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS` during a metered outage.** Lines 485-493 compute the due interval, but line 493 polls when `due or metered is None or metered * 5 >= THRESHOLD_USD * 4`. When CloudWatch metering is unavailable, `metered is None` is true on every five-minute Lambda tick, so the slow Cost Explorer path is forced on every tick. This contradicts the module's own comment at lines 49-54 that CE is not polled every tick.\n\n**3. `DRY_RUN` release emits a notification that contradicts the returned attachment state.** `_apply(False)` returns `[]` without touching IAM when `DRY_RUN` is true at lines 412-420. The release path still publishes `Bedrock daily cap released` at lines 562-569, and the returned `deny_attached` value re-reads live IAM at line 599. A dry-run release can therefore announce detachment while reporting the deny policy is still attached.\n\n## Resolved design decisions\n\nFor a Cost Explorer period with no `Total`, treat the reading as `0.0`, the same convention already used when `ResultsByTime` is empty at lines 354-356. The function signature is `float`, the handler already has a separate `ClientError` path for unavailable CE, and a present period with no cost data means no billed Bedrock spend for that period rather than transport failure.\n\nFor CE polling, remove the unconditional `metered is None` trigger. A metered outage must not suppress a due CE poll, but it also must not override `CE_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS`; the retained triggers are due interval and near-threshold metered spend.\n\nFor dry-run release, do not publish `Bedrock daily cap released` when no detach happened. `_apply()` is intentionally a no-op in dry-run mode, so the authoritative observable state is the live IAM state returned by `_is_attached()`. Announcing a release without a detach is the misleading branch.\n\n## Testing seam\n\nAdd the tests to `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py`. Use the existing import seam in `load_handler()` and `FakeAWS.client()` at test lines 162-245 to inject fake `boto3` clients for IAM, SSM, Cost Explorer, CloudWatch, and SNS. Extend only those fakes when a test needs to count calls or return a Cost Explorer shape not currently covered.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_ce_spend_today_empty_total_returns_zero` drives `_ce_spend_today` with `FakeCE(results_by_time=[{\"Total\": {}}])` and gets `0.0` with no `KeyError` under `pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -k test_ce_spend_today_empty_total_returns_zero`.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_unavailable_meter_respects_ce_min_interval` runs two handler ticks with `metered=None`, same-day cached CE state, and `ce_last_poll` inside `CE_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS`, and observes exactly zero new `FakeCE.get_cost_and_usage` calls under `pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -k test_unavailable_meter_respects_ce_min_interval`.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_unavailable_meter_polls_ce_after_interval` advances `ce_last_poll` beyond `CE_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS` while `metered=None` and observes exactly one fresh Cost Explorer call under `pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -k test_unavailable_meter_polls_ce_after_interval`.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_dry_run_release_does_not_publish_detach_notification` starts with all targets attached, runs the below-threshold release branch with `DRY_RUN=true`, and observes `deny_attached is True`, no IAM detach calls, and no `Bedrock daily cap released` SNS subject under `pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -k test_dry_run_release_does_not_publish_detach_notification`.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py` contains all 4 tests named above and they pass together with the file's existing cases.\n- [x] [non-codebase] `make verify` exits 0.\n      provenance: environment=GitHub Actions hosted runner, gating `ubuntu-latest, py3.13` matrix cell; principal=GitHub Actions CI on Gerrit change 2994; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the gating cell selects `not integration and not external`, the same set `make test` selects, and it voted `Verified +1` on the revision that was submitted.\n\n## Testing\n\nRun `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -k 'ce_spend_today_empty_total_returns_zero or unavailable_meter_respects_ce_min_interval or unavailable_meter_polls_ce_after_interval or dry_run_release_does_not_publish_detach_notification'` during development, then run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py`, and finally run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify` before push.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nThe Terraform module findings from the same review stay separate. The main release guard at line 562 must not gain release-on-outage behavior; a signal outage keeps an existing deny attached.\n\n## Verification evidence\n\nFix landed as Gerrit change 2994 and is present at the tip of `main` (`bd8c1c4ced7`). Verification was run against a throwaway worktree detached at `origin/main`, so no local edits could influence the result.\n\nAll 4 named tests exist in the landed tree and pass individually:\n\n```\ntests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_ce_spend_today_empty_total_returns_zero PASSED\ntests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_unavailable_meter_respects_ce_min_interval PASSED\ntests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_unavailable_meter_polls_ce_after_interval PASSED\ntests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_dry_run_release_does_not_publish_detach_notification PASSED\n4 passed, 49 deselected in 1.10s\n```\n\nThe whole file passes: `53 passed in 63.11s`.\n\nOnly the `make verify` criterion is tagged `[non-codebase]`: it names no repository path, and its evidence is a command's exit status in CI rather than anything recoverable from the snapshot.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py","reason":"Fix `_ce_spend_today`, the Cost Explorer poll gate, and dry-run release notification/response behavior."},{"path":"tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py","reason":"Add unit coverage for CE no-data periods, outage poll throttling, due CE polling, and dry-run release consistency using the existing FakeAWS boto3 seam."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","d635-9e7f-2bea-4ebe"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"d0759e9b-7637-48bc-b53f-eefef0e544fe","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"604c-ade8-0ae3-4dd7","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Bedrock spend-cap handler: CE no-data KeyError, rate limit bypassed during outage, and a self-contradicting DRY_RUN release","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4dd5da81-06d5-48b4-96dc-28fc5e0ca247","4a3ffc9a-4406-4b76-8646-b60d7091cf30","cb58ffa3-3c02-4353-af22-6c92660f0d60","a09424ce-52e0-478b-8699-2dcc4c144289","0ebc62f1-5c67-4d4f-9394-a47904a7a62d","934b883f-c76d-4f1b-9bc5-b4afdb6ef90b","3d9a26cd-6831-4a66-ae2e-7fe7888391b4","fca05450-ee39-475d-805e-99ca1c41be1c","d0759e9b-7637-48bc-b53f-eefef0e544fe","389d9636-00b4-468a-8d65-446a365f5b26","9084618e-d36d-4053-ab5b-81b7e4a6ec32"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1789893068408848451,"uuid":"60e083c5-91f3-4bf7-ab5c-ef5716132de1"}